notes_for_next_subtask:
pay.rs: pub fn attempt_output(&Attempt, Broadcast) -> Value (frozen pay/rebroadcast shape); fn broadcast_exit(Broadcast)->u8 (Accepted 0, else 3), private, so make it pub(crate) or reuse the match for rebroadcast;
pub fn pay_guard(&StateDir, id) -> Result<Option<(Value,u8)>,(u8,&str)> validates the id, then read_attempt; runs before chain.connect();
pub async fn pay(state, &dyn ChainFactory, &Path, id, delta) -> crate::CommandResult; main.rs pay() delegates to it.
CommandResult is now Result<(Value, exit_code), (code, err)>: tx_status/rebroadcast must return (json, code).
After write_attempt the only step is chain::broadcast, which cannot error, so post-attempt exits are always 0 or 3.
Probe pitfall: StateDir needs a 0700 parent for --state-dir; `mkdir -m 700 -p a/b` leaves a at the umask mode, so chmod both levels.
